/home/ubuntu/workspace/geometry-of-dln-fibre/expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/threads/21-hdiv-achiever/codex/mechanism-answer.md:3:**Q2.** REQUIRES-CHART, or at least requires a geometric substitute that compares `F` to the achiever monomial on a positive-measure parametrized region. **DERIVED:** The listed squeeze machinery equates point RLCTs only; it does not produce flat-coordinate box integrals, boundary divergence, or a map from monomial chart coordinates into `cubeBox N ε`. **DERIVED:** Since the general-M achiever family is only combinatorial exponent data, `monomialIntegrand_lintegral_box_eq_top` cannot be pushed to `F` without geometric realization. **DERIVED:** The single-global `phiUnit` route is unavailable by #6/#7. **GENERAL-KNOWLEDGE:** A composed sequence of local blow-ups along the achiever path is the natural resolution-theoretic escape: it need not be one miraculous triangular chart, but it must still come with Jacobian control and a pullback upper bound of the right monomial type. **DERIVED:** For divergence, the needed inequality direction is `|F ∘ φ| ≤ C · monomial`, since then `|F ∘ φ|^{-c'} ≥ C^{-c'} · monomial^{-c'}`.
/home/ubuntu/workspace/geometry-of-dln-fibre/expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/threads/21-hdiv-achiever/codex/mechanism-answer.md:5:**Q3.** Tractability ranking for Lean: (c) first if the smooth-block `Φ` has an already-computable box divergence theorem in flat coordinates; otherwise (a) first; (b) last. **DERIVED:** (c) load-bearing sub-lemma: `∀ c' ≥ t, ∀ ε>0, ∫ cubeBox ε ofReal (Φ x)^{-c'} = ⊤`, plus a neighborhood inequality `F ≤ C·Φ` on a box. **DERIVED:** (a) load-bearing sub-lemma: a measurable wedge/tube parametrization with positive transverse measure and `F` bounded above by the critical monomial model, so Fubini reduces to the divergent one-dimensional or monomial integral. **DERIVED:** (b) load-bearing sub-lemma: existence of an achiever blow-up chart `φ` mapping a parameter box into the flat cube, with measurable change-of-variables/Jacobian factor and `|F ∘ φ| ≤ C·monomial` with the exponent data of the achieving leaf. **GENERAL-KNOWLEDGE:** A full chart is conceptually standard but Lean-heavy because it packages geometry, measure pushforward, Jacobian, and pullback asymptotics.
