/home/ubuntu/workspace/geometry-of-dln-fibre/expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/29-geometry-assembly-ladder/codex/nugget-answer.md:5:Reason: in characteristic `p`, `G` can act transitively on a smooth open orbit while the orbit map has zero differential. Example: `𝔾ₐ` acts on `𝔸¹` by `t • x = x + t^p`. The orbit of `0` is all `𝔸¹`, but `d(t ↦ t^p)_0 = 0`. So “open dense transitive orbit + smooth closure” does not imply `range dμ = T_O`.
/home/ubuntu/workspace/geometry-of-dln-fibre/expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/29-geometry-assembly-ladder/codex/nugget-answer.md:7:Thus stabilizer smoothness/separability is not cosmetic; it is exactly what excludes this pathology.
