/home/ubuntu/workspace/geometry-of-dln-fibre/expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/threads/32-r1-general-hdiv-design/codex/cost-answer.md:5:The determinant is the load-bearing certificate tying the chart to `leafH p = minAdm - 1`, the monomial threshold, and the `cov` Jacobian weight. `HasFDerivAt` is large, but mostly compositional once the chart is expressed through reusable maps; `cov` is annoying but finite-measure bookkeeping. The determinant needs a general block-triangular/composition proof over fin-indexed path cases, and the facts show the spectator monomial is construction-sensitive, so it cannot be safely faked or globally hand-waved.
/home/ubuntu/workspace/geometry-of-dln-fibre/expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/threads/32-r1-general-hdiv-design/codex/cost-answer.md:11:A wedge comparison could aim to prove on a positive-measure box sector that `routeMCore M (psi u) <= C*u^2` with a product-measure set in spectator variables, then integrate `u^{-minAdm}` against a known volume factor. But to get the codimension exponent `minAdm - 1`, one still needs the correct transverse-volume scaling, which is exactly what the chart Jacobian encodes. So unless the alternative proves that scaling by a simpler Fubini/box-volume construction, it just reintroduces the determinant under another name.
